{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UVMpfiqV7KCUspPFwqFP9D","type":"tool_result","content":"690\t  string spoolPath, sockPath, runId, pipe;\n691\t  // Who this event belongs to. Both answers were already in the gate's hands\n692\t  // on every invocation and neither one reached the disk.\n693\t  //\n694\t  // `call` is Claude Code's tool_use_id, which arrives on both the PreToolUse\n695\t  // and the PostToolUse hook for one tool call. Every hook invocation is its\n696\t  // own process, so `run` is unique per EVENT and correlates nothing —\n697\t  // measured on the live spool, 75.126 events carried 75.126 distinct run ids,\n698\t  // zero reuse. STEP_START and STEP_OK are the two ends of one tool call and\n699\t  // nothing written down said so. Pairing them by \"the next OK in the same\n700\t  // pipe\" closes 58,5% of the starts and joins unrelated work in 17,6% of even\n701\t  // those, giving a p99 of 15,5 minutes and one pair five days wide. Duration\n702\t  // is not missing from this ledger, it is unjoinable, and this id is the join.\n703\t  //\n704\t  // `sess` is the session id. `pipe` is spelled \"<project>:session\" and is not\n705\t  // one — it is the directory, so every session and every subagent that has\n706\t  // ever run in stitchu/ shares a single pipe spanning 214 hours across nine\n707\t  // days. rabadon-export turns a pipe into a TRACE id, which means a trace is\n708\t  // currently the entire history of a folder.\n709\t  string call, sess;\n710\t  bool drill;\n711\t  int seq = 0;\n712\t  int sockFd = -1;\n713\t\n714\t  void open_sock() {\n715\t    sockFd = socket(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0);\n716\t    if (sockFd < 0) return;\n717\t    fcntl(sockFd, F_SETFL, O_NONBLOCK);\n718\t    struct sockaddr_un addr; memset(&addr, 0, sizeof(addr));\n719\t    addr.sun_family = AF_UNIX;\n720\t    strncpy(addr.sun_path, sockPath.c_str(), sizeof(addr.sun_path) - 1);\n721\t    if (connect(sockFd, (struct sockaddr*)&addr, sizeof(addr)) < 0 && errno != EINPROGRESS) {\n722\t      close(sockFd); sockFd = -1;\n723\t    }\n724\t  }\n725\t\n726\t  void emit(const string& ev, const string& extraJson) {\n727\t    string body = \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"seq\\\":\" + std::to_string(++seq) +\n728\t      \",\\\"ts\\\":\" + std::to_string(now_ms()) +\n729\t      \",\\\"run\\\":\\\"\" + runId + \"\\\",\\\"pipe\\\":\\\"\" + json_escape(pipe) + \"\\\",\\\"ev\\\":\\\"\" + ev + \"\\\"\" +\n730\t      // Absent rather than empty. A hook that carries no tool_use_id (Stop,\n731\t      // SessionStart) is not part of a tool call, and writing \"\" would make\n732\t      // every one of them look like members of the same nameless call.\n733\t      (call.empty() ? \"\" : \",\\\"call\\\":\\\"\" + json_escape(call) + \"\\\"\") +\n734\t      (sess.empty() ? \"\" : \",\\\"sess\\\":\\\"\" + json_escape(sess) + \"\\\"\") +\n735\t      (extraJson.empty() ? \"\" : \",\" + extraJson) +\n736\t      (drill ? \",\\\"drill\\\":true\" : \"\");\n737\t    // hash-chained ledger: every event carries prev = SHA-256 of the previous\n738\t    // event line in this day file and the .head sidecar commits the last hash\n739\t    // AND the line count, so the spool is TAMPER-EVIDENT — edit, drop, truncate\n740\t    // or re-stitch any line and `rabadon audit` names the break. One writer for\n741\t    // all three binaries: chain.h.\n742\t    string line = rbchain::append(spoolPath, body);\n743\t    if (sockFd >= 0) { ssize_t r = write(sockFd, line.c_str(), line.size()); (void)r; }\n744\t  }\n745\t\n746\t  ~Emitter() { if (sockFd >= 0) close(sockFd); }\n747\t};\n748\t\n749\t// ---------- rules ----------"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1af7ad45-1899-4b3a-984d-f407428731b5","uuid":"b1f37eab-4499-4e7c-b067-efbd766a37b7","timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:34:30.098Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/native/gate.cpp","content":"  string spoolPath, sockPath, runId, pipe;\n  // Who this event belongs to. Both answers were already in the gate's hands\n  // on every invocation and neither one reached the disk.\n  //\n  // `call` is Claude Code's tool_use_id, which arrives on both the PreToolUse\n  // and the PostToolUse hook for one tool call. Every hook invocation is its\n  // own process, so `run` is unique per EVENT and correlates nothing —\n  // measured on the live spool, 75.126 events carried 75.126 distinct run ids,\n  // zero reuse. STEP_START and STEP_OK are the two ends of one tool call and\n  // nothing written down said so. Pairing them by \"the next OK in the same\n  // pipe\" closes 58,5% of the starts and joins unrelated work in 17,6% of even\n  // those, giving a p99 of 15,5 minutes and one pair five days wide. Duration\n  // is not missing from this ledger, it is unjoinable, and this id is the join.\n  //\n  // `sess` is the session id. `pipe` is spelled \"<project>:session\" and is not\n  // one — it is the directory, so every session and every subagent that has\n  // ever run in stitchu/ shares a single pipe spanning 214 hours across nine\n  // days. rabadon-export turns a pipe into a TRACE id, which means a trace is\n  // currently the entire history of a folder.\n  string call, sess;\n  bool drill;\n  int seq = 0;\n  int sockFd = -1;\n\n  void open_sock() {\n    sockFd = socket(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0);\n    if (sockFd < 0) return;\n    fcntl(sockFd, F_SETFL, O_NONBLOCK);\n    struct sockaddr_un addr; memset(&addr, 0, sizeof(addr));\n    addr.sun_family = AF_UNIX;\n    strncpy(addr.sun_path, sockPath.c_str(), sizeof(addr.sun_path) - 1);\n    if (connect(sockFd, (struct sockaddr*)&addr, sizeof(addr)) < 0 && errno != EINPROGRESS) {\n      close(sockFd); sockFd = -1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  void emit(const string& ev, const string& extraJson) {\n    string body = \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"seq\\\":\" + std::to_string(++seq) +\n      \",\\\"ts\\\":\" + std::to_string(now_ms()) +\n      \",\\\"run\\\":\\\"\" + runId + \"\\\",\\\"pipe\\\":\\\"\" + json_escape(pipe) + \"\\\",\\\"ev\\\":\\\"\" + ev + \"\\\"\" +\n      // Absent rather than empty. A hook that carries no tool_use_id (Stop,\n      // SessionStart) is not part of a tool call, and writing \"\" would make\n      // every one of them look like members of the same nameless call.\n      (call.empty() ? \"\" : \",\\\"call\\\":\\\"\" + json_escape(call) + \"\\\"\") +\n      (sess.empty() ? \"\" : \",\\\"sess\\\":\\\"\" + json_escape(sess) + \"\\\"\") +\n      (extraJson.empty() ? \"\" : \",\" + extraJson) +\n      (drill ? \",\\\"drill\\\":true\" : \"\");\n    // hash-chained ledger: every event carries prev = SHA-256 of the previous\n    // event line in this day file and the .head sidecar commits the last hash\n    // AND the line count, so the spool is TAMPER-EVIDENT — edit, drop, truncate\n    // or re-stitch any line and `rabadon audit` names the break. One writer for\n    // all three binaries: chain.h.\n    string line = rbchain::append(spoolPath, body);\n    if (sockFd >= 0) { ssize_t r = write(sockFd, line.c_str(), line.size()); (void)r; }\n  }\n\n  ~Emitter() { if (sockFd >= 0) close(sockFd); }\n};\n\n// ---------- rules ----------","numLines":60,"startLine":690,"totalLines":4658}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeLnvMUVbzrGFbdWCx3Pb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0147fqG1bSpR4WLcYcNjRRus","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2\necho \"=== bus.mjs socket path ===\"; grep -nE 'sock|SOCK|path|tmpdir|join' core/bus.mjs | head -25\necho; echo \"=== bus.mjs listen/bind region 240-290 ===\"; sed -n '240,290p' core/bus.mjs","description":"Find bus.mjs socket path"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1729,"cache_read_input_tokens":57672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1729},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1af7ad45-1899-4b3a-984d-f407428731b5","uuid":"7a4879fb-b9ca-46a7-825d-f9adfc6a5581","request_id":"req_011CeLnvLhc3qetFCjXxAUPb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0147fqG1bSpR4WLcYcNjRRus","type":"tool_result","content":"=== bus.mjs socket path ===\n6:// happens, over a unix domain socket, to any attached `rabadon watch`.\n12://      to a local spool file, and the number of socket drops is COUNTED and\n19:// Topology: `rabadon watch` OWNS the socket (server). Pipelines are clients:\n25:import path from 'node:path';\n29:export const RABADON_DIR = process.env.RABADON_DIR || path.join(os.homedir(), '.rabadon');\n30:export const SOCK_PATH = process.env.RABADON_SOCK || path.join(RABADON_DIR, 'rabadon.sock');\n31:export const SPOOL_DIR = path.join(RABADON_DIR, 'spool');\n115: * (newline included) so the caller can fan the same bytes to the socket.\n158:  path.join(SPOOL_DIR, `${day}.jsonl`);\n189:  let sock = null;\n190:  let sockUp = false;\n196:    sock = net.connect(SOCK_PATH);\n197:    sock.on('connect', () => {\n198:      sockUp = true;\n199:      for (const line of preBuffer.splice(0)) sock.write(line);\n201:    sock.on('error', () => { sockUp = false; sock = null; dropped += preBuffer.length; preBuffer.length = 0; });\n202:    sock.on('close', () => { sockUp = false; sock = null; });\n203:    sock.unref(); // the socket must never keep the pipeline process alive\n205:    sock = null;\n212:    // spool first — the spool is the source of truth, the socket is the live\n219:    if (sock && sockUp) {\n221:        const ok = sock.write(line);\n223:      } catch { dropped++; sockUp = false; }\n224:    } else if (sock && !sockUp) {\n234:  emit.stats = () => ({ dropped, live: sockUp });\n\n=== bus.mjs listen/bind region 240-290 ===\n * Start the watch server (used by `rabadon watch`). Owns the socket.\n * onEvent(event, meta) is called for every parsed event from every pipeline.\n * Returns { close }.\n */\nexport function listen(onEvent) {\n  ensureDirs();\n  // a stale socket file from a killed watcher would block bind — remove it,\n  // but only if nothing is actually listening on it\n  if (fs.existsSync(SOCK_PATH)) {\n    const probe = net.connect(SOCK_PATH);\n    const stale = new Promise((resolve) => {\n      probe.on('error', () => resolve(true));   // nobody home -> stale file\n      probe.on('connect', () => { probe.end(); resolve(false); });\n    });\n    return stale.then((isStale) => {\n      if (!isStale) throw new Error(`rabadon watch: another watcher already owns ${SOCK_PATH}`);\n      fs.unlinkSync(SOCK_PATH);\n      return bind(onEvent);\n    });\n  }\n  return Promise.resolve(bind(onEvent));\n}\n\nfunction bind(onEvent) {\n  const server = net.createServer((conn) => {\n    let buf = '';\n    conn.on('data', (chunk) => {\n      buf += chunk;\n      let nl;\n      while ((nl = buf.indexOf('\\n')) !== -1) {\n        const line = buf.slice(0, nl);\n        buf = buf.slice(nl + 1);\n        if (!line.trim()) continue;\n        try { onEvent(JSON.parse(line)); } catch { onEvent({ v: 1, ev: 'UNPARSEABLE', raw: line.slice(0, 200) }); }\n      }\n    });\n    conn.on('error', () => { /* a pipeline dying mid-line is normal, not our error */ });\n  });\n  server.listen(SOCK_PATH);\n  return {\n    close: () => new Promise((r) => server.close(() => { try { fs.unlinkSync(SOCK_PATH); } catch { } r(); })),\n  };\n}\n\nexport default { emitter, listen, EV, SOCK_PATH, RABADON_DIR };","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1af7ad45-1899-4b3a-984d-f407428731b5","uuid":"62bb5fa2-b17a-488d-bd3e-8e4ebaf6367e","timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:34:31.606Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== bus.mjs socket path ===\n6:// happens, over a unix domain socket, to any attached `rabadon watch`.\n12://      to a local spool file, and the number of socket drops is COUNTED and\n19:// Topology: `rabadon watch` OWNS the socket (server). Pipelines are clients:\n25:import path from 'node:path';\n29:export const RABADON_DIR = process.env.RABADON_DIR || path.join(os.homedir(), '.rabadon');\n30:export const SOCK_PATH = process.env.RABADON_SOCK || path.join(RABADON_DIR, 'rabadon.sock');\n31:export const SPOOL_DIR = path.join(RABADON_DIR, 'spool');\n115: * (newline included) so the caller can fan the same bytes to the socket.\n158:  path.join(SPOOL_DIR, `${day}.jsonl`);\n189:  let sock = null;\n190:  let sockUp = false;\n196:    sock = net.connect(SOCK_PATH);\n197:    sock.on('connect', () => {\n198:      sockUp = true;\n199:      for (const line of preBuffer.splice(0)) sock.write(line);\n201:    sock.on('error', () => { sockUp = false; sock = null; dropped += preBuffer.length; preBuffer.length = 0; });\n202:    sock.on('close', () => { sockUp = false; sock = null; });\n203:    sock.unref(); // the socket must never keep the pipeline process alive\n205:    sock = null;\n212:    // spool first — the spool is the source of truth, the socket is the live\n219:    if (sock && sockUp) {\n221:        const ok = sock.write(line);\n223:      } catch { dropped++; sockUp = false; }\n224:    } else if (sock && !sockUp) {\n234:  emit.stats = () => ({ dropped, live: sockUp });\n\n=== bus.mjs listen/bind region 240-290 ===\n * Start the watch server (used by `rabadon watch`). Owns the socket.\n * onEvent(event, meta) is called for every parsed event from every pipeline.\n * Returns { close }.\n */\nexport function listen(onEvent) {\n  ensureDirs();\n  // a stale socket file from a killed watcher would block bind — remove it,\n  // but only if nothing is actually listening on it\n  if (fs.existsSync(SOCK_PATH)) {\n    const probe = net.connect(SOCK_PATH);\n    const stale = new Promise((resolve) => {\n      probe.on('error', () => resolve(true));   // nobody home -> stale file\n      probe.on('connect', () => { probe.end(); resolve(false); });\n    });\n    return stale.then((isStale) => {\n      if (!isStale) throw new Error(`rabadon watch: another watcher already owns ${SOCK_PATH}`);\n      fs.unlinkSync(SOCK_PATH);\n      return bind(onEvent);\n    });\n  }\n  return Promise.resolve(bind(onEvent));\n}\n\nfunction bind(onEvent) {\n  const server = net.createServer((conn) => {\n    let buf = '';\n    conn.on('data', (chunk) => {\n      buf += chunk;\n      let nl;\n      while ((nl = buf.indexOf('\\n')) !== -1) {\n        const line = buf.slice(0, nl);\n        buf = buf.slice(nl + 1);\n        if (!line.trim()) continue;\n        try { onEvent(JSON.parse(line)); } catch { onEvent({ v: 1, ev: 'UNPARSEABLE', raw: line.slice(0, 200) }); }\n      }\n    });\n    conn.on('error', () => { /* a pipeline dying mid-line is normal, not our error */ });\n  });\n  server.listen(SOCK_PATH);\n  return {\n    close: () => new Promise((r) => server.close(() => { try { fs.unlinkSync(SOCK_PATH); } catch { } r(); })),\n  };\n}\n\nexport default { emitter, listen, EV, SOCK_PATH, RABADON_DIR };","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
